</li>
<li data-start=3D"4265" data-end=3D"4294">
<p data-start=3D"4267" data-end=3D"4294"><code data-start=3D"4267" data-end=
=3D"4294">("project", "life_years")</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4297" data-end=3D"4337">
<p data-start=3D"4299" data-end=3D"4337"><code data-start=3D"4299" data-end=
=3D"4337">("parameters", "project_life_years")</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4340" data-end=3D"4378">
<p data-start=3D"4342" data-end=3D"4378"><code data-start=3D"4342" data-end=
=3D"4378">("Financing_Terms", "tenor_years")</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4380" data-end=3D"4398">So there are gaps:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4400" data-end=3D"4775">
<li data-start=3D"4400" data-end=3D"4562">
<p data-start=3D"4402" data-end=3D"4562"><code data-start=3D"4402" data-end=
=3D"4430">project.project_life_years</code> and <code data-start=3D"4435" d=
ata-end=3D"4464">Financing_Terms.tenor_years</code> are <strong data-start=
=3D"4469" data-end=3D"4481">required</strong> by the schema registry, but <=
strong data-start=3D"4510" data-end=3D"4528">not considered</strong> by <co=
de data-start=3D"4532" data-end=3D"4561">_extract_project_life_years</code>=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4563" data-end=3D"4775">
<p data-start=3D"4565" data-end=3D"4775">If someone uses <code data-start=
=3D"4581" data-end=3D"4610">Financing_Terms.tenor_years</code> (which your =
RequiredFieldSpec explicitly allows), the schema guard will be happy, but <=
code data-start=3D"4697" data-end=3D"4726">_extract_project_life_years</cod=
e> will fall through to the heuristic and may fail.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4777" data-end=3D"4888">Fix: make <code data-start=3D"4787=
" data-end=3D"4816">_extract_project_life_years</code> and <code data-start=
=3D"4821" data-end=3D"4848">_register_cashflow_schema</code> use the <stron=
g data-start=3D"4857" data-end=3D"4875">same path list</strong>. Easiest is=
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4890" data-end=3D"5106">
<li data-start=3D"4890" data-end=3D"5027">
<p data-start=3D"4892" data-end=3D"5027">Add <code data-start=3D"4896" data=
-end=3D"4931">("project", "project_life_years")</code> and <code data-start=
=3D"4936" data-end=3D"4972">("Financing_Terms", "tenor_years")</code> to <c=
ode data-start=3D"4976" data-end=3D"5005">_extract_project_life_years</code=
>=E2=80=99 explicit candidates.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5028" data-end=3D"5106">
<p data-start=3D"5030" data-end=3D"5106">Or better: define a single constan=
t list of paths and use it in both places.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"5108" data-end=3D"5151">3. Duplicated utils vs <code data=
-start=3D"5136" data-end=3D"5151">finance.utils</code></h4>
<p data-start=3D"5153" data-end=3D"5190">You now have two families of helpe=
rs:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5192" data-end=3D"5335">
<li data-start=3D"5192" data-end=3D"5244">
<p data-start=3D"5194" data-end=3D"5209">In this module:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5212" data-end=3D"5244">
<li data-start=3D"5212" data-end=3D"5244">
<p data-start=3D"5214" data-end=3D"5244"><code data-start=3D"5214" data-end=
=3D"5224">as_float</code>, <code data-start=3D"5226" data-end=3D"5238">get_=
nested</code>, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5245" data-end=3D"5335">
<p data-start=3D"5247" data-end=3D"5266">In <code data-start=3D"5250" data-=
end=3D"5265">finance.utils</code>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5269" data-end=3D"5335">
<li data-start=3D"5269" data-end=3D"5335">
<p data-start=3D"5271" data-end=3D"5335"><code data-start=3D"5271" data-end=
=3D"5281">as_float</code>, <code data-start=3D"5283" data-end=3D"5295">get_=
nested</code>, used by <code data-start=3D"5305" data-end=3D"5314">metrics<=
/code> and <code data-start=3D"5319" data-end=3D"5334">epc_breakdown</code>=
.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5337" data-end=3D"5486">That=E2=80=99s survivable but dang=
erous long-term: if someone changes the behaviour (e.g. default handling) i=
n one place, you get subtle divergences between:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5488" data-end=3D"5570">
<li data-start=3D"5488" data-end=3D"5520">
<p data-start=3D"5490" data-end=3D"5520">CFADS layer (this module), and</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5521" data-end=3D"5570">
<p data-start=3D"5523" data-end=3D"5570">KPI &amp; EPC helpers (<code data-=
start=3D"5542" data-end=3D"5551">metrics</code>, <code data-start=3D"5553" =
data-end=3D"5568">epc_breakdown</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5572" data-end=3D"5695">If you want a =E2=80=9Chard=E2=80=
=9D design principle: <strong data-start=3D"5611" data-end=3D"5678">cashflo=
w, debt, irr define behaviour; utils just centralise it.</strong> In practi=
ce I=E2=80=99d:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5697" data-end=3D"5907">
<li data-start=3D"5697" data-end=3D"5754">
<p data-start=3D"5699" data-end=3D"5754">Move these helper implementations =
into <code data-start=3D"5738" data-end=3D"5753">finance.utils</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5755" data-end=3D"5907">
<p data-start=3D"5757" data-end=3D"5907">Import them from there in this mod=
ule, to make sure cashflow, debt, metrics, EPC, etc. all share a single can=
onical <code data-start=3D"5873" data-end=3D"5883">as_float</code>/<code da=
ta-start=3D"5884" data-end=3D"5896">get_nested</code> behaviour.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5909" data-end=3D"5997">Not urgent for passing tests, but =
I would clean this before expanding the model further.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"5999" data-end=3D"6062">4. Bottom-of-file self-test / sch=
ema registration is messy</h4>
<p data-start=3D"6064" data-end=3D"6115">Right now the tail of the file is =
structurally off:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6117" data-end=3D"6400">
<li data-start=3D"6117" data-end=3D"6222">
<p data-start=3D"6119" data-end=3D"6222">You define <code data-start=3D"613=
0" data-end=3D"6145">sample_config</code> and an <code data-start=3D"6153" =
data-end=3D"6181">if __name__ =3D=3D "__main__":</code> block <strong data-=
start=3D"6188" data-end=3D"6197">above</strong> the schema registration.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6223" data-end=3D"6400">
<p data-start=3D"6225" data-end=3D"6400">Then you define <code data-start=
=3D"6241" data-end=3D"6268">_register_cashflow_schema</code>, run it in a <=
code data-start=3D"6282" data-end=3D"6303">try: / except: pass</code>, and =
<strong data-start=3D"6309" data-end=3D"6333">inside that <code data-start=
=3D"6323" data-end=3D"6331">except</code></strong> body you=E2=80=99ve past=
ed a whole bunch of <code data-start=3D"6370" data-end=3D"6393">print("SELF=
-TEST...")</code> stuff.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6402" data-end=3D"6413">That means:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6415" data-end=3D"6684">
<li data-start=3D"6415" data-end=3D"6596">
<p data-start=3D"6417" data-end=3D"6596">The pretty CFADS self-test at the =
bottom will only ever run <strong data-start=3D"6477" data-end=3D"6510">if =
schema registration throws</strong> and only then, inside that <code data-s=
tart=3D"6538" data-end=3D"6546">except</code> block. That=E2=80=99s almost =
certainly not what you want.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6597" data-end=3D"6684">
<p data-start=3D"6599" data-end=3D"6684">It also makes the module harder to=
 reason about and a bit brittle for linters / IDEs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6686" data-end=3D"6694">I would:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6696" data-end=3D"6847">
<li data-start=3D"6696" data-end=3D"6796">
<p data-start=3D"6698" data-end=3D"6796">Keep <code data-start=3D"6703" dat=
a-end=3D"6732">_register_cashflow_schema()</code> and the <code data-start=
=3D"6741" data-end=3D"6760">try: _register...</code> block near the top (af=
ter imports).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6797" data-end=3D"6847">
<p data-start=3D"6799" data-end=3D"6847">Move <em data-start=3D"6804" data-=
end=3D"6809">all</em> self-test code into a proper, single:</p>
</li>
</ul>
