<p data-start=3D"6142" data-end=3D"6401">Even a =E2=80=9Csingle-shot=E2=80=
=9D principal_series <code data-start=3D"6180" data-end=3D"6194">[debt_tota=
l]</code> is better than zero for equity IRR =E2=80=93 as long as tests are=
 built around that definition. If you care about timing accuracy, we can de=
rive principal drawdowns from the construction drawdown schedules instead.<=
/p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6403" data-end=3D"6480">(B) Units and naming: you=E2=80=
=99re treating everything as USD but not saying so</h3>
<p data-start=3D"6482" data-end=3D"6505">Throughout this module:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6507" data-end=3D"6724">
<li data-start=3D"6507" data-end=3D"6534">
<p data-start=3D"6509" data-end=3D"6534">Capex =3D <code data-start=3D"6517=
" data-end=3D"6534">capex.usd_total</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6535" data-end=3D"6647">
<p data-start=3D"6537" data-end=3D"6647">Debt totals, tranches and IDC are =
effectively <strong data-start=3D"6583" data-end=3D"6590">USD</strong> amou=
nts (despite logs saying <code data-start=3D"6620" data-end=3D"6628">$%.2fM=
</code> with raw numbers).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6648" data-end=3D"6724">
<p data-start=3D"6650" data-end=3D"6724"><code data-start=3D"6650" data-end=
=3D"6670">debt_service_total</code>, <code data-start=3D"6672" data-end=3D"=
6690">debt_outstanding</code>, <code data-start=3D"6692" data-end=3D"6708">=
cfads_extended</code> are all in USD.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6726" data-end=3D"6756">That=E2=80=99s <strong data-start=
=3D"6733" data-end=3D"6741">fine</strong>, but it means:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6758" data-end=3D"6938">
<li data-start=3D"6758" data-end=3D"6828">
<p data-start=3D"6760" data-end=3D"6828">The metrics module=E2=80=99s expec=
tation of <code data-start=3D"6796" data-end=3D"6803">*_usd</code> is conce=
ptually correct.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6829" data-end=3D"6938">
<p data-start=3D"6831" data-end=3D"6938">Your naming in the return dict cou=
ld be clearer to avoid confusion with any future LKR-layer debt analysis.</=
p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6940" data-end=3D"6958">I=E2=80=99d minimally fix:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6960" data-end=3D"7115">
<li data-start=3D"6960" data-end=3D"7037">
<p data-start=3D"6962" data-end=3D"7037">Log messages (<code data-start=3D"=
6976" data-end=3D"6996">"Principal $%.2fM"</code> is misleading unless you =
divide by 1e6).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7038" data-end=3D"7115">
<p data-start=3D"7040" data-end=3D"7115">Set the <code data-start=3D"7048" =
data-end=3D"7054">_usd</code> aliases as above so analytics &amp; workbooks=
 can rely on those.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"7117" data-end=3D"7166">(C) DSCR series length vs CFADS s=
eries length</h3>
<p data-start=3D"7168" data-end=3D"7210">This is more of a design quirk tha=
n a bug:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7212" data-end=3D"7357">
<li data-start=3D"7212" data-end=3D"7276">
<p data-start=3D"7214" data-end=3D"7276"><code data-start=3D"7214" data-end=
=3D"7227">dscr_series</code> is 23 periods (construction + transition + ops=
).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7277" data-end=3D"7357">
<p data-start=3D"7279" data-end=3D"7357">CFADS in metrics for IRR/NPV is pu=
rely from <code data-start=3D"7323" data-end=3D"7336">annual_rows</code> (y=
ears of ops only).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"7359" data-end=3D"7379">That=E2=80=99s okay because:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7381" data-end=3D"7600">
<li data-start=3D"7381" data-end=3D"7436">
<p data-start=3D"7383" data-end=3D"7436">The <strong data-start=3D"7387" da=
ta-end=3D"7398">IRR/NPV</strong> logic doesn=E2=80=99t care about DSCR leng=
th.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7437" data-end=3D"7600">
<p data-start=3D"7439" data-end=3D"7496">The <strong data-start=3D"7443" da=
ta-end=3D"7457">DSCR stats</strong> in <code data-start=3D"7461" data-end=
=3D"7470">metrics</code> clean the DSCR series by:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7499" data-end=3D"7600">
<li data-start=3D"7499" data-end=3D"7539">
<p data-start=3D"7501" data-end=3D"7539">Dropping <code data-start=3D"7510"=
 data-end=3D"7516">None</code>, NaN, <code data-start=3D"7523" data-end=3D"=
7528">inf</code>, and &lt;=3D 0.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7542" data-end=3D"7600">
<p data-start=3D"7544" data-end=3D"7600">So your <code data-start=3D"7552" =
data-end=3D"7557">inf</code> for non-service periods is ignored anyway.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"7602" data-end=3D"7707">But: if at some point you want DSC=
R charts that line up exactly with years in <code data-start=3D"7680" data-=
end=3D"7693">annual_rows</code>, we=E2=80=99d either:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7709" data-end=3D"7899">
<li data-start=3D"7709" data-end=3D"7772">
<p data-start=3D"7711" data-end=3D"7772">derive a pure =E2=80=9Cops-only DS=
CR series=E2=80=9D at the metrics layer, or</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7773" data-end=3D"7899">
<p data-start=3D"7775" data-end=3D"7899">change ScenarioAnalytics <code dat=
a-start=3D"7800" data-end=3D"7819">_build_dataframes</code> to merge <code =
data-start=3D"7829" data-end=3D"7845">cfads_extended</code> + <code data-st=
art=3D"7848" data-end=3D"7868">debt_service_total</code> directly into <cod=
e data-start=3D"7883" data-end=3D"7898">timeseries_df</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"7901" data-end=3D"8145">Right now, ScenarioAnalytics falls=
 back to a scalar DSCR line per scenario (using dscr_min) if no per-period =
DSCR exists in <code data-start=3D"8025" data-end=3D"8038">annual_rows</cod=
e>. With this debt module, that behaviour is still consistent: DSCR charts =
will show a flat line at dscr_min.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"8147" data-end=3D"8186">(D) Unused / half-used config kno=
bs</h3>
<p data-start=3D"8188" data-end=3D"8230">A few parameters are currently dec=
orative:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"8232" data-end=3D"8485">
<li data-start=3D"8232" data-end=3D"8319">
<p data-start=3D"8234" data-end=3D"8319"><code data-start=3D"8234" data-end=
=3D"8247">grace_years</code> is read but never used; everything is driven o=
ff <code data-start=3D"8297" data-end=3D"8318">interest_only_years</code>.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8320" data-end=3D"8485">
<p data-start=3D"8322" data-end=3D"8485">Construction schedule is described=
 as capex-oriented, but you don=E2=80=99t cross-check or normalise percenta=
ges; you just use <code data-start=3D"8441" data-end=3D"8464">drawdown_pct_=
per_year</code> to scale total debt.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"8487" data-end=3D"8519">Not fatal, but good to be aware:</=
p>
<ul data-start=3D"8521" data-end=3D"8793">
<li data-start=3D"8521" data-end=3D"8633">
<p data-start=3D"8523" data-end=3D"8633">If you want lending/credit people =
to trust this, either wire <code data-start=3D"8584" data-end=3D"8597">grac=
e_years</code> into the schedule logic or drop it.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8634" data-end=3D"8793">
<p data-start=3D"8636" data-end=3D"8793">If you want consistency with the c=
apex curve, we can derive drawdown percentages from <code data-start=3D"872=
2" data-end=3D"8745">construction_schedule</code> instead of taking separat=
e <code data-start=3D"8773" data-end=3D"8792">debt_drawdown_pct</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"8795" data-end=3D"8798">
<h2 data-start=3D"8800" data-end=3D"8848">4. Interaction with the irr archi=
tecture rule</h2>
<p data-start=3D"8850" data-end=3D"8923">You flagged earlier (and I have in=
 memory) that the architecture rule is:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"8925" data-end=3D"8998">
<p data-start=3D"8927" data-end=3D"8998">IRR/NPV must live only in <code da=
ta-start=3D"8953" data-end=3D"8969">finance/irr.py</code>, and NOT in metri=
cs modules.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"9000" data-end=3D"9064">This debt module respects that: it=
 doesn=E2=80=99t touch IRR/NPV at all.</p>
<p data-start=3D"9066" data-end=3D"9177">The inconsistency lives in <strong=
 data-start=3D"9093" data-end=3D"9104">metrics</strong>, where <code data-s=
tart=3D"9112" data-end=3D"9121">npf.irr</code> and <code data-start=3D"9126=
" data-end=3D"9135">npf.npv</code> are currently called directly. That will=
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"9179" data-end=3D"9372">
<li data-start=3D"9179" data-end=3D"9246">
<p data-start=3D"9181" data-end=3D"9246">Violate the =E2=80=9CIRR-only-in-f=
inance.irr=E2=80=9D architecture test we wrote.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9247" data-end=3D"9372">
<p data-start=3D"9249" data-end=3D"9372">Conceptually blur responsibilities=
: valuation logic should be in <code data-start=3D"9314" data-end=3D"9327">=
finance.irr</code> and metrics should just consume its outputs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"9374" data-end=3D"9570">So debt is not the offender here =
=E2=80=93 metrics is. But since you explicitly said =E2=80=9Creevaluate oth=
er modules against these three=E2=80=A6 debt, cashflow, irr=E2=80=9D, I=E2=
=80=99m calling it out so we fix it in the same sweep.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"9572" data-end=3D"9575">
