<li data-start=3D"1236" data-end=3D"1349">
<p data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1349">Trim/comment the now-trivial shim =
modules in <code data-start=3D"1284" data-end=3D"1310">dutchbay_v14chat/fin=
ance</code> so they=E2=80=99re clearly =E2=80=9Clegacy path only=E2=80=9D.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1514">
<p data-start=3D"1355" data-end=3D"1514">Add one tiny test asserting that <=
code data-start=3D"1388" data-end=3D"1441">dutchbay_v14chat.finance.irr.irr=
 is finance.irr.irr</code> (purely to guard someone =E2=80=9Chelpfully=E2=
=80=9D re-implementing stuff there later).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1517" data-end=3D"1653">
<p data-start=3D"1520" data-end=3D"1653">In a later sprint, tighten coverag=
e focus even more on v14 modules in <code data-start=3D"1590" data-end=3D"1=
602">pytest.ini</code> (you=E2=80=99ve already mostly done this via <code d=
ata-start=3D"1640" data-end=3D"1651">testpaths</code>).</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1655" data-end=3D"1891" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-onl=
y-node=3D"">For now though: you=E2=80=99ve got a passing, coverage-complian=
